t  completely faithful to the plot he has  planned  otherwise the show would have to run  another 5 seasons he said  what all of this means is that the  ending and fates of most of the key  characters will be the same  then it will descend into madness bran  will become the king  but it's the journey to this point that  will be entirely different pacing build  up characters  everything up until the end will be  quite different before this revelation  from dnd came out i said in my season 8  episode 6 review video that  i don't think the ending is necessarily  bad as in fact it's how george r  martin's books will also end  as they said multiple times that the  ending will be the same but the journey  to get there will be quite different  and the journey is exactly what was so  disappointing in the show  danny going mad bran becoming the king  and everything else could have been  written so that all of this would make  sense  instead we got a rushed and poorly  written season branding is nowhere near  bittersweet only better  i have no doubt that george r martin  will make all of this make sense  and most importantly it will not be  rushed who has a better story than brand  broken tyrion says and for some reason  everyone accepts it  as a valid argument and they proclaim  bran the king  why would they do that he has no better  claim than anyone else  he doesn't even have the best story  among them and he did nothing of great  significance in the war against the  night king  more like brando useless the reasoning  seemed weak  and the lack of setup is apparent what  it shows us is that dnd knew they had to  make bran the king  but had no idea how to make it happen  had no idea how to write his stories  had no idea how to make him one of the  most important characters in the show  which is actually why bran was not even  present throughout the entire season 5  and which is ultimately why the ending  was bad they failed to deliver bran's  journey to becoming the king  to talk about bran's journey in the  books and how will he become one of the  most important characters we firstly  need to understand george r martin's  mind  every important character and event  martin writes is based on the actual  history  from real events to myths and legends  the entire race song of ice and fire is  inspired by the wars of the roses  a series of english civil wars for  control of the throne  the houses and characters from those  wars are what inspired most houses and  characters in game of thrones  most of the characters have their  historical equivalent some of the most  shocking moments in tv history such as  the red wedding has historical parallels  as well  even some of the most epic battles are  inspired by real historical battles such  as the battle of blackwater  which is based on the second arab siege  of constantinople  where greek fire was used to repel the  invaders as it could remain lit on water  just like wildfire was used so now that  we know george armor uses historical  characters events myths and legends to  inspire his own events and characters  we need to ask ourselves on who is bran  stark based  surely the most important martin's  character must be based on someone or  something as most other things are  well some fans might have guessed it  right bran is most likely based on the  fisher king also known as the wounded  king  because much like bran a known warrior  wounded him  and he is unable to father next  generation to carry on after his death  which is one of the main points bran was  chosen a king to make things even more  interesting  in celtic mythology the fisher king is  derived from the figure of brand of  blessed  and the name bran in welsh is usually  translated as crow  or raven which oddly matches with brain  and him being the three-eyed raven  george r martin once said that the fan  theory got the ending right  and few fans became confident that they  now know which one it is  bran is the fisher king it's a story in  which the king is wounded and then  blessed by divine power  the fisher king is the last in a long  bloodline charged with keeping the holy  grail  much like brain is charged by the  three-eyed raven from the very beginning  by appearing in his dreams as a raven to  come to him become him and  keep the power of the three-eighth raven  on his way to holy land to find the holy  grail  fisher king was encountered by three  knights bran stark on his way to find  the triad raven is encountered by three  threats as well  firstly by the wildings where he had to  work hodor and the direwolves to avoid  being found and killed  then he encountered the man of the  night's watch at crassur's keep  where he was captured but managed to  escape and finally for the third time he  was encountered by whites  in front of the 3 8 raven's cave who  were plays there for one purpose  and it's to prevent him from entering it  and becoming the three-eyed raven  as already said the fisher king has many  similarities with brain  from the characters itself to their  fates and journey and names the  nicknames  bryn stark was always supposed to be the  king he is the only type of monarch  george r martin sees fit to rule the  kind where the king suffers on his  journey  and is almost dehumanized for the sake  of his people  in the show brain rules from the red  keep yet the iron throne is destroyed  in the books it's most likely that brain  will rule from harehole  and the great council where they choose  the king will take place not at the  dragonpit  but at harehole this makes far more  sense in the books given the  significance of herreral succession and  lordship  it was here where the previous great  council was held when all the lords  chose and voted for the targaryen  successor  then king jaehaerys first targaryen was  not certain who his successor should be  carrying hole is located on the shore of  the gods eye the largest lake where the  pact between the first men and the  children of the forest was signed on the  isle of faces  carrick hall is also centrally located  being in the middle of westeros  so i think bran will rule from harehole  not king's landing  one of the big differences george armarn  will make that will lead to bran  becoming the king  is bran playing the biggest role in  defeating white walkers  the long night was not really long in  the show it lasted only one night  bran stark did not showcase any of his  powers have no doubt that the books will  deliver on the horrors that were set up  and the white walkers will not be  defeated in a single night  the long night in the books is the event  that will completely change everything  the others the dragons greenseers and  skinchangers  red priests faceless men and undead of  all types  we will see them all play a big role how  will it lead to brand broken  well bran will play the biggest role in  defeating the white walkers  and i believe that will win him the  throne there's one interesting quote  stannis gives to jon snow in the books  stannis says lord seaworth is a man of  humble birth  but he reminded me of my duty when all i  could think of was my rights  i had the card before the horse that was  said i was trying to win the throne to  save the kingdom  when i should have been trying to save  the kingdom to win the throne  george r martin did said this logic of  true king being the one who saves his  people  and what better king than bran who saves  the realm from the long night  after the war for the dawn people will  look at those who save them as their new  leaders  i believe dany will descend into madness  and die but the books will do it much  better than the show did  i believe jon who will be another hero  of the long knight will be offered to be  the king on the great council  on the grounds of him being not only a  hero but the one with the best claim  but he will refuse just like his great  great unclaemon targaryen did  and will go far north removing himself  from political court  the only and the most important hero  left will be brand broken  and he will be chosen a king after a  long council all in all i believe the  books will make bran's journey to  becoming the king satisfying  and more importantly i believe there  will be clues and hints pointing towards  it but the show gave us only a few that  most viewers probably did not even  notice  one particular moment in the pilot seems  significant in retrospect  camera cuts to young brain during ned  stark's recitation of the execution oath  just as ned says the line in the name of  robert of the house baratheon the first  of his name king of the andals and the  first men  camera cuts to brain whom jon tells not  to look away  it seems they left it purposely unclear  whether we should focus on brain or john  in that shot  that's the tactic the show often uses to  subvert our expectations  for example after heart home it seemed  that the night king was after jon  when in fact it was brand that he really  wanted it seems significant that bran is  also the first person we see targeted by  jaime lannister  the man infamously known as kingslayer  trying to slay this king before he even  becomes one  tyrion approaches brain in season 8  episode 4 at the victory celebration  following the battle of winterfell he  compliments bran's wheelchair  saying it's even better than the saddle  he designed back in season one  according to bran his cherries based on  the one darren targaryen built for his  nephew 120 years ago  bran is talking about darren ii  targaryen known as their on the good  he made the wheelchair for his sister  daenerys targaryen's crippled son  his familiarity with that history  impresses tyrion  who told joffrey back in season 4 that  their own story should be required  reading for any future ruler  quote the lives of the four kings grand  maester kate's history of the reigns  of darren the young dragon baler the  blessed aegon the unworthy  and they are on the good a book every  king should read  in conclusion the game of thrones  showrunners confirmed that george  armard's books will land the same  especially the brand becoming the king  part however this doesn't mean we will  be left bitter and disappointed  just because the show failed to deliver  satisfying journey towards descending  dany going mad bran becoming the king  and everything else could have been  written so that all of this would make  sense instead of being rushed  poorly written and bitter i have no  doubt that george armard will make all  of this make sense  give bran stark a good story a good  journey and make him useful  and make him the most important  character in the long night  i believe it will get a satisfying and  bitter sweet ending in the books  and i really look forward to bran  stark's story thank you guys so much for  watching i hope you enjoyed this video  and if you did please give it a big  thumbs up and i hope to see you in the  next one peace

